<title>JAPAN: FORECAST-Breakdown of June 'tankan' forecasts.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Breakdown of June 'tankan' forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of updated forecasts by private think-tanks for diffusion indices for major manufacturers and non-manufacturers in the Bank of Japan's June quarterly corporate survey, known as the &quot;tankan&quot;.</p>
<p>The think-tanks were polled by Reuters on Monday. Initial forecasts, obtained last week, are in parentheses in those cases where revisions were made. Three institutions made downward revisions and the rest were unchanged.</p>
<p>The tankan is due to be released at 8.50 a.m. on Wednesday (2350 GMT Tuesday).</p>
<p>			    Major mfrs	    Major non-mfrs</p>
<p>March actual		 +2			-6</p>
<p>March forecast</p>
<p>    for June		 -1			-7</p>
<p>*******************************************************</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers	    -2			-7</p>
<p>HSBC James Capel	    0			-8</p>
<p>BZW			    +1			-3</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch		+3			-3</p>
<p>Salomon Bros		 -3			-10</p>
<p>Schroders		    +3			-7</p>
<p>ING Barings		  -3 (+2)		 -9 (-5)</p>
<p>JP Morgan		    +4			-6</p>
<p>CS First Boston	    -2*		     -5*</p>
<p>BOT-Mitsubishi	     +2 (+4)		 -4 (-4)</p>
<p>Securities</p>
<p>IBJ			    +1			-7</p>
<p>DKB Research		 +3			-5</p>
<p>Fuji Research		-3			-9</p>
<p>Sanwa Research	     -4			-8</p>
<p>Nihon Research	     -2			-7</p>
<p>Sakura Securities	  +1 (+2)		 -5 (-4)</p>
<p>*CS First Boston's economist was not available to comment on a possible revision.</p>
